...
}*ptr;

isc_mem_t*mctx;

isc_mem_putanddetach(&ptr->mctx,ptr,sizeof(*ptr));

is the equivalent of:
mctx=NULL;
isc_mem_attach(ptr->mctx,&mctx);
isc_mem_detach(&ptr->mctx);
isc_mem_put(mctx,ptr,sizeof(*ptr));
isc_mem_detach(&mctx);

These functions are actually implemented in isc__mem_<function> (two underscores). The single-underscore macros are used to pass FILE and LINE, and in the case of the put functions, to set the pointer being freed to NULL in the calling function.
